@_ods_cext.register_operation(_Dialect)
class GetArrivalCountOp(_ods_ir.OpView):
  r"""
  Computes the number of mbarrier arrivals that one logical release
  (`lir.producer_commit` for the producer side, `lir.consumer_release`
  for the consumer side) contributes to a barrier of the pipeline:
  
    count = dedup_arrives * arrives_per_cta * fan_in
  
  The result feeds `lir.create_pipeline` / `lir.create_pipeline_with_mask`
  as the producer/consumer arrival count, which is why the op takes the
  pipeline TYPE rather than a pipeline value: the pipeline does not exist
  yet when its counts are computed. During `lir-pipeline-to-nvvm` the op
  is rewritten to `sync.get_arrival_count` on the edge built from the
  pipeline type by the same mapping that builds the pipeline's own
  release/acquire edges, so the supplied count and the arrives the
  lowering emits agree by construction.
  
  - `op_subset` selects a subset of the side's operation types, for split
    producers or consumers where one release op covers part of the work
    (e.g. ST_SHARED on one warp and UMMA on another). Absent covers the whole
    side.
  - `num_threads_per_cta` is the number of threads per CTA that issue the
    release op. With `elect_one_sync` (mirroring the release ops' flag),
    one thread per warp arrives, so the count is divided by the warp
    size. LIR's elect-one requires full warp participation (see
    `lir.producer_commit`): the issuing threads must form complete,
    converged warps, so `num_threads_per_cta` must be a multiple of the
    warp size (a caller contract -- it may be a runtime value, so it is
    not verified).
  - `elect_leader_cta` (mirroring the release ops' flag) marks a release
    that only the leader CTA of each CTA pair executes; for a
    pair-converging pipeline the fan-in drops from 2 to 1. It is also
    accepted where leader-only issuance is inherent and the count is
    unaffected: multicast-masked arrivals, and the all-2CTA-TMA producer
    edge (whose per-CTA arrive convention only ever observes the leader
    CTA's slot).
  - `fan_in` overrides the number of CTAs converging on the barrier when
    the pipeline-derived value does not apply. Pipelines whose arrivals
    are multicast-masked have no derivable fan-in (the mask is not a
    query input): the caller must supply the converging-issuer count,
    e.g. `popcount(mask) / cta_count` as a runtime value or the
    structural multicast participant count.
  
  The elect flags exist so callers can mirror their release ops
  verbatim. A caller that already knows the resolved execution shape may
  equivalently pass resolved values -- e.g. `num_threads_per_cta = 1`
  with no flags for a release executed by a single elected thread.
  
  The result is the contribution of ONE logical arrival, not a barrier's
  total expected count. Multiplicity belongs to the caller: it invokes
  the query once per logical arrival that lands in one phase and sums the
  results.
  """

